<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="cid:css-5513614b-41c1-467f-85df-6494eaddd0e2@mhtml.blink" /><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="cid:css-84a2979d-9880-46cb-bfa4-622781cfa3ae@mhtml.blink" /><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="cid:css-4840263d-1456-4ec8-a46d-6f8fcb1152fa@mhtml.blink" /><meta http-equiv="x-dns-prefetch-control" content="off" data-html-viewer-injected=""><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" data-html-viewer-injected="">

<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Marie &amp; Pierre Curie: 10 Tons to 0.1 Grams (1898–1902)</title>

</head>
<body>
<div class="app">
  <!-- Clean Top Bar -->
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="title-wrap">
      <h1>Marie &amp; Pierre Curie (1898–1902)</h1>
      <span class="pill-tag">10 Tons Rock → 0.1 g Pure Radium</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-dots">
      <button class="stage-chip active" id="nav0" data-eh="_eh0">1. Boil Ore</button>
      <button class="stage-chip" id="nav1" data-eh="_eh1">2. Dump Mud</button>
      <button class="stage-chip" id="nav2" data-eh="_eh2">3. Split Po/Ra</button>
      <button class="stage-chip" id="nav3" data-eh="_eh3">4. Crystallize</button>
      <button class="stage-chip" id="nav4" data-eh="_eh4">5. Pure Vial</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Main Stage -->
  <main class="stage">
    <!-- Left: Story Banner + Shed Scene + Bottom Dock -->
    <section class="left-col">
      <div class="bench-wrap">
        <div class="story-banner">
          <div class="story-box">
            <div class="story-kicker" id="stepKicker">Step 1 of 5 • Boiling 10 Tons of Rock</div>
            <div class="story-heading" id="stepHeading">Dissolve Pitchblende Ore in Boiling Acid</div>
            <div class="story-desc" id="stepDesc">Pitchblende is 4× more radioactive than uranium—proving tiny traces of unknown elements are locked inside the rock.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="story-box highlight">
            <div class="story-kicker">Why Is Marie Stirring?</div>
            <div class="story-heading" id="whyHeading">To Pull Invisible Atoms Out of Solid Rock</div>
            <div class="story-desc" id="whyDesc">Stirring in boiling acid dissolves radium &amp; polonium into the liquid (colored dots) while heavy waste mud (grey dots) sinks.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="canvas-holder">
          <canvas id="shedCanvas" width="1513" height="1244"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dock">
        <div class="dock-group">
          <span class="dock-label">Element:</span>
          <button id="raBtn" class="btn active" data-eh="_eh5">Radium (Ra)</button>
          <button id="poBtn" class="btn" data-eh="_eh6">Polonium (Po)</button>
        </div>

        <div class="dock-group">
          <button id="autoStirBtn" class="btn amber" data-eh="_eh7" style="opacity: 1;">Auto-Stir: OFF</button>
          <button id="quizToggleBtn" class="btn quiz-btn" data-eh="_eh8">Check-In Quiz (0/3)</button>
          <button class="btn" data-eh="_eh9">Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Right: Detector + Collected Material + Big Hours Counter + Key -->
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <span>Pierre's Radiation Meter</span>
          <span id="activityBadge" class="badge" style="color: var(--radium);">4× Uranium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meter-wrap">
          <canvas id="meterCanvas" width="686" height="257"></canvas>
        </div>

        <div class="collected-hero">
          <div class="collected-label" id="collectedTitle">Collected Pure Radium (RaCl₂)</div>
          <div class="collected-value" id="collectedValue" style="color: rgb(148, 163, 184);">0.0000 g (None yet)</div>
          <div class="collected-sub" id="collectedSub">Still locked inside 10,000 kg of raw rock</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Enlarged Hours of Stirring Readout -->
        <div class="hours-hero">
          <div class="hours-left">
            <div class="hours-label">Hours of Stirring</div>
            <div class="hours-big" id="hoursStat">0 hrs</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cycles-pill">
            <div class="cycles-lbl">Crystal Cycles</div>
            <div class="cycles-val" id="crystStat">0 / 400</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card legend-card">
        <div class="card-header" style="margin-bottom:2px;">
          <span>What You're Seeing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="legend-row">
          <span class="dot" id="activeDot" style="background:var(--radium); box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--radium);"></span>
          <span id="activeDotLabel"><b>Green Dots:</b> Radium dissolving into acid</span>
        </div>
        <div class="legend-row">
          <span class="dot" style="background:#78716c;"></span>
          <span><b>Grey Dots:</b> Useless rock mud sinking to bottom</span>
        </div>
        <div class="legend-row">
          <span class="dot" style="background:var(--amber);"></span>
          <span><b>Stirring:</b> Drag Marie's rod or use <b>Auto-Stir</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </main>

  <!-- Student Check-In Modal -->
  <div id="quizModal" class="modal-backdrop" data-eh="_eh10">
    <div class="modal-box">
      <div class="modal-head">
        <h2>Student Check-In: The Curies' Discovery</h2>
        <button class="btn" data-eh="_eh11">Back to Lab ✕</button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body" id="quizBody"><div class="q-card"><div class="q-title">1. Why did Marie Curie have to stir the boiling pitchblende ore for hours every day?</div><div class="q-opts"><button class="opt-btn">To melt solid rock into pure liquid uranium metal.</button><button class="opt-btn">To dissolve tiny amounts of radium and polonium out of the rock into the acid so waste mud could be thrown away.</button><button class="opt-btn">To cool the mixture down before Pierre tested it.</button></div><div class="q-feedback"></div></div><div class="q-card"><div class="q-title">2. How much pure radium chloride did the Curies collect from 10,000 kg (10 tons) of ore?</div><div class="q-opts"><button class="opt-btn">About 100 kg (3 full sacks)</button><button class="opt-btn">About 10 kg (a heavy brick)</button><button class="opt-btn">Just 0.1 grams (a tiny glowing speck at the bottom of a glass vial)</button></div><div class="q-feedback"></div></div><div class="q-card"><div class="q-title">3. What two brand-new radioactive elements did Marie and Pierre Curie discover in pitchblende?</div><div class="q-opts"><button class="opt-btn">Polonium (named after Poland) and Radium</button><button class="opt-btn">Uranium and Thorium</button><button class="opt-btn">Barium and Bismuth</button></div><div class="q-feedback"></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>



